title: the argument in brief
pid: 4b18a7ef-59f9-44c1-ab05-941bff909f27
body: |2-
  - the few few hundred that Cortes led took a population in the millions
  - a minor tech difference made all the difference:
    horses and steel swords
  - both sides were deeply divided
  - guns didn't really help much
  - even after the diseases the numbers were shockingly tilted against the Spanish
